.\" Man page for mandible itself (spec §15). Hand-written rather than
.\" generated (clap_mangen is not in the project's dependency table, and
.\" the CLI surface is small enough that hand-maintenance is cheap); keep
.\" this in sync with mandible/src/cli.rs when flags change.
.TH MANDIBLE 1 "2026-08-06" "mandible 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mandible \- a universal, interactive TUI reference for CLI tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mandible
.I TOOL
.RB [ \-\-refresh ]
.br
.B mandible
.B \-\-doctor
.I TOOL
.RB [ \-\-refresh ]
.br
.B mandible
.B \-\-completions
.I SHELL
.br
.B mandible
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mandible
opens a full-screen, explorable tree of every command, subcommand, and
flag that
.I TOOL
has, with descriptions rather than just names, plus a fuzzy search bar
that finds a flag from a partial memory of its name or purpose.
.PP
It is a
.B reference browser,
not a command builder:
.B mandible
never executes
.I TOOL
itself, and never runs the command you're looking up. Its job ends the
moment you have found the right flag and can copy its exact spelling
with
.BR y .
.PP
Structure and descriptions are assembled from whichever of several
extraction tiers apply to
.IR TOOL ,
merged field-by-field by trust (structural accuracy vs. prose quality),
never by which tier happened to run first. Tiers include a curated
third-party command-spec catalog, a general-purpose
.B \-\-help
grammar, shell completion-script parsing, and native dynamic probes
(cobra's
.BR __complete ,
clap's
.BR CompleteEnv ),
merged and cached per tool. See
.B mandible \-\-doctor
.I TOOL
for exactly which tiers contributed to a given tool's tree, and the
project's own
.I spec.md
for the full design.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I TOOL
The tool to open, e.g.
.IR git .
Resolved against
.BR PATH .
Required unless
.B \-\-doctor
is given.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor \fITOOL\fR
Print a non-interactive extraction report for
.I TOOL
instead of opening the TUI: which tiers detected and succeeded, node
and flag counts, the percentage of flags with a description, the
vendored catalog's commit and vendoring date (if it contributed), and
elapsed time. Exits non-zero if no tier produced anything.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Bypass the on-disk cache for this invocation, re-run extraction from
scratch, and repopulate the cache with the fresh result. Use this if a
tool was upgraded and mandible still shows the old structure.
.TP
.B \-\-completions \fISHELL\fR
Print a shell completion script for
.I SHELL
to stdout and exit.
.I SHELL
is one of
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
.BR fish ,
.BR elvish ,
or
.BR powershell .
Packaged builds (`.deb`/`.rpm`) already install completions to the
standard per-distro paths; this flag is for
.B cargo install
users and anyone scripting their own setup, e.g.:
.RS
.PP
.nf
mandible \-\-completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_mandible
.fi
.RE
.TP
.B \-h\fR,\fB \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.B \-V\fR,\fB \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
Shown in-app via
.BR ? .
.TP
.BR "Up/Down" ", " k / j
Move the tree selection.
.TP
.BR "Right arrow" ", " Enter ", " l
Expand the selected node (extracting its children on first expand).
.TP
.BR "Left arrow" ", " h
Collapse the selected node, or jump to its parent if already collapsed.
.TP
.B /
Focus the search bar.
.TP
.B Esc
Leave the search bar, keeping the filter pinned; press again to clear it.
.TP
.B Tab
Switch focus between the tree and detail panes.
.TP
.B y
Copy the selected flag's exact spelling, or the selected node's full
command path, to the clipboard.
.TP
.B r
Re-extract the current tool, bypassing the cache.
.TP
.B .
Toggle display of hidden and deprecated items.
.TP
.B q\fR, \fBCtrl-C
Quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MANDIBLE_LOG
Enables diagnostic logging (a
.I tracing
.B EnvFilter
directive string, e.g.
.IR debug " or " mandible_extract=trace ),
written to stderr — never to the TUI's own terminal output.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to any value, mandible degrades its single accent color to
bold/reverse/underline only.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME
Standard XDG base-directory variables; mandible respects them for its
on-disk cache and user override files. See
.B FILES
below for the resolved defaults, which differ on macOS.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/mandible/
(Linux, default \fI~/.cache/mandible/\fR; macOS:
\fI~/Library/Caches/mandible/\fR) — the on-disk extraction cache,
gzip-compressed JSON, one file per tool. Safe to delete entirely; it is
rebuilt on next use.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mandible/overrides/<tool>.toml
(Linux, default \fI~/.config/mandible/overrides/\fR; macOS:
\fI~/Library/Application Support/mandible/overrides/\fR) — optional,
user-local, per-tool override files (highest authority on both
structure and prose). Never distributed with mandible itself.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
No extraction tier could produce a result for the given tool, stdout is
not a tty and the TUI could not open, or an argument error.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full design documentation, including the extraction-tier model and
caching/invalidation rules, ships in the project repository as
.IR spec.md .
.SH AUTHORS
Sadig Akhund and contributors.
